1
00:01:39,039 --> 00:01:41,240
If you want to stand firm in this position,

2
00:01:41,759 --> 00:01:43,200
hard work alone

3
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:44,800
isn't enough.

4
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:47,479
Because everyone else works hard too.

5
00:01:47,840 --> 00:01:50,200
I'd better go get that information for Nannalin.

6
00:01:50,479 --> 00:01:51,800
Yeah, see you later.

7
00:01:54,120 --> 00:01:55,440
Your heart is beating so fast.

8
00:01:57,640 --> 00:01:59,960
I'm sorry Ratee arrived early.

9
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:01,880
Not at all.

10
00:02:02,120 --> 00:02:03,240
It's really a pleasure.

11
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:04,520
Please, have a seat.

12
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:06,640
It is rather strange.

13
00:02:07,040 --> 00:02:10,120
Someone as meticulous and ambitious as Ratee...

14
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:13,160
Why would she hire an agency like ours?

15
00:02:49,400 --> 00:02:50,880
Yes, Ms. Nannalin?

16
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:52,720
I've arrived at the multibrand store.

17
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,240
What do you see?

18
00:02:55,400 --> 00:02:57,800
Overall, it looks good. The store is beautiful.

19
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,960
I'll take another look around,

20
00:02:59,960 --> 00:03:01,880
then send you my report right away.

21
00:03:02,520 --> 00:03:05,280
Pick up the items and come straight back to the office.

22
00:03:05,760 --> 00:03:06,320
Okay?

23
00:03:06,480 --> 00:03:07,320
Understood.

24
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:50,520
Oh my goodness, Pim!

25
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:54,320
Look at our rookie! She's all grown up now!

26
00:03:54,640 --> 00:03:56,120
You're right!

27
00:03:56,960 --> 00:03:58,760
I have to agree with Nui.

28
00:03:58,760 --> 00:04:01,400
Alice looks so much better today.

29
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:04,680
Her scheduling and desk organization...

30
00:04:04,680 --> 00:04:07,400
She looks so professional and ready to work.

31
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,240
Well done!

32
00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:11,200
Thank you, Pim and Nui.

33
00:04:11,200 --> 00:04:13,640
This time, I've made myself a promise.

34
00:04:13,640 --> 00:04:16,800
I won't be as disorganized as I was before.

35
00:04:16,800 --> 00:04:18,519
I promise I won't be disorganized again. I'm giving this my all!

36
00:04:19,279 --> 00:04:20,200
Fabulous!

37
00:04:20,519 --> 00:04:22,960
Then organize mine too, will you?

38
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:27,120
Don't celebrate too soon, Alice.

39
00:04:30,840 --> 00:04:32,360
Remember one thing.

40
00:04:32,360 --> 00:04:33,920
In the real working world,

41
00:04:33,920 --> 00:04:36,040
work tends to come at you

42
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:38,760
with the biggest, most urgent problems

43
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:42,280
just when you think you have everything under control.

44
00:04:51,920 --> 00:04:53,000
Back to work, darling.

45
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:55,200
Let's get to work.

46
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:06,160
Get to work.

47
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:07,840
You, darling. Get back to work.

48
00:05:20,240 --> 00:05:21,760
Your morning hot tea,

49
00:05:21,760 --> 00:05:24,440
and this week's schedule summary.

50
00:05:24,720 --> 00:05:26,520
I've organized your appointments

51
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:29,200
and allowed time for the meetings.

52
00:05:50,440 --> 00:05:51,400
The tea is too weak.

53
00:05:52,200 --> 00:05:53,560
And the schedule is too packed.

54
00:05:56,040 --> 00:05:59,120
Oolong tea needs hotter water to steep properly.

55
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:02,800
Otherwise, its astringent aroma won't come out.

56
00:06:04,160 --> 00:06:05,160
As for the schedule,

57
00:06:05,760 --> 00:06:09,720
you've booked three major campaign meetings back-to-back

58
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:13,080
without giving the team any time

59
00:06:13,080 --> 00:06:15,080
to discuss potential issues.

60
00:06:15,720 --> 00:06:18,080
I wouldn't call that time management.

61
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,280
I'd call it sending the team into battle unprepared.

62
00:06:28,320 --> 00:06:29,320
I'm sorry.

63
00:06:29,560 --> 00:06:31,400
I'll revise it as quickly as possible.

64
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,040
Go adjust the schedule,

65
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:49,240
and add these tasks as well.

66
00:06:49,760 --> 00:06:51,040
Review every detail of the deck

67
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:53,800
for Ratee's cosmetics brand.

68
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,960
Make sure it meets the standards we agreed on.

69
00:06:59,640 --> 00:07:02,840
And coordinate the mood and tone with the creative team.

70
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:06,760
Shortlist some more A-list KOLs

71
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:08,480
and add five backup names.

72
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:15,640
I want everything on my desk before my afternoon meeting.

73
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:20,400
Any questions?

74
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:23,120
No.

75
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:25,440
I'll make all the revisions perfectly.

76
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:56,200
Alice.

77
00:07:57,480 --> 00:07:59,000
Can I ask you something?

78
00:07:59,320 --> 00:08:00,360
Well...

79
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:03,440
Does being a content creator mean

80
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:05,680
you have to come up with and write every word yourself?

81
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:09,840
Of course.

82
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:11,560
I mean...

83
00:08:11,800 --> 00:08:13,240
For content work,

84
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,960
we have to do the research,

85
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:16,840
plan out the storytelling,

86
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,720
and write all the captions and articles ourselves.

87
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:24,240
We have to make sure the brand image

88
00:08:24,320 --> 00:08:25,800
comes together perfectly.

89
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:27,720
Ugh!

90
00:08:28,520 --> 00:08:31,560
I thought there'd be a support team to write it all.

91
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:34,679
Writing all day sounds exhausting.

92
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,840
Just staring at a screen and typing all day...

93
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:40,159
Oh,

94
00:08:40,240 --> 00:08:41,080
how boring!

95
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:04,560
Pim, let's go to the meeting room.

96
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:35,200
Alice.

97
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:36,880
Can I ask you a favor?

98
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:38,720
Mm-hmm.

99
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:41,320
Could you take a look...

100
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:45,160
at my caption for the cosmetics campaign?

101
00:09:45,160 --> 00:09:47,320
I've put together a rough draft, but

102
00:09:47,640 --> 00:09:49,440
I'm not sure if it's any good.

103
00:10:01,120 --> 00:10:02,640
Here's the thing, Mueanfun.

104
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:05,680
Ratee's cosmetics brand

105
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:08,640
is meant to feel expensive and sophisticated.

106
00:10:09,040 --> 00:10:11,680
So the language and captions

107
00:10:11,880 --> 00:10:14,240
need to be nuanced,

108
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:16,680
refined, and understated,

109
00:10:16,880 --> 00:10:19,000
with a sense of mature confidence.

110
00:10:21,560 --> 00:10:25,040
We can't use trendy teenage slang

111
00:10:25,040 --> 00:10:28,640
or pushy, hard-sell promotional language.

112
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:29,960
That just won't work.

113
00:10:31,160 --> 00:10:33,840
Otherwise, everything the brand has built

114
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:35,800
could fall apart in an instant.

115
00:10:37,200 --> 00:10:38,400
Hmm...

116
00:10:38,840 --> 00:10:41,560
I thought we'd just use words that make people buy it.

117
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:43,240
That should be enough, really.

118
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,320
Office work is so complicated.

119
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,600
Isn't she kind?

120
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,720
I really admire how kind Alice is.

121
00:11:32,080 --> 00:11:33,760
She's already buried in work,

122
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:35,840
yet she still makes time

123
00:11:35,840 --> 00:11:38,280
to rescue Mueanfun's awful campaign keywords.

124
00:11:38,680 --> 00:11:39,640
That girl...

125
00:11:39,640 --> 00:11:41,200
She acts like the chairman's granddaughter.

126
00:11:42,080 --> 00:11:44,200
A high-class content creator!

127
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:46,800
But do you know what content she watches all day?

128
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:50,720
Online shopping! Choosing suit colors all day, swipe, swipe!

129
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:52,200
She's been at it since nine this morning.

130
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:53,720
Keep your voice down, Nui.

131
00:11:53,960 --> 00:11:55,960
Seriously, Nui, don't mock her so much. Someone might hear us.

132
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:58,600
If somebody walks by and hears us,

133
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:00,080
we'll be in trouble again.

134
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:05,840
But your comparison was pretty accurate.

135
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:09,000
Content in her online shopping cart!

136
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:10,520
You're wicked!

137
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:20,920
Being kind is a good thing, Alice.

138
00:12:21,560 --> 00:12:23,200
Helping your coworkers

139
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:24,200
isn't wrong at all.

140
00:12:25,720 --> 00:12:28,680
But remember this important boundary.

141
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,720
You can help them,

142
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:35,480
but don't help so much that everyone at the company starts believing

143
00:12:35,480 --> 00:12:37,200
that what you're doing

144
00:12:37,200 --> 00:12:39,320
is actually your responsibility.

145
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:54,800
As for the content section,

146
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:56,400
I think

147
00:12:56,640 --> 00:12:59,840
we should make short, viral-style videos, like...

148
00:13:00,240 --> 00:13:01,600
the kind young people love.

149
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:02,760
And use hashtags

150
00:13:03,040 --> 00:13:04,840
that are trending right now.

151
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:06,080
I guarantee

152
00:13:06,440 --> 00:13:08,520
our engagement will skyrocket.

153
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:12,000
Brilliant, right?

154
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:13,840
Isn't it brilliant?

155
00:13:14,120 --> 00:13:14,920
It'll go through the roof!

156
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:20,560
Well,

157
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:22,800
what Mueanfun is suggesting

158
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:24,240
is probably

159
00:13:24,240 --> 00:13:27,800
to use the energy of short-form video,

160
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:31,280
but adapt the storytelling to a quiet luxury mood.

161
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:34,440
Instead of using generic trending hashtags,

162
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:38,640
we could focus on polished lighting and composition

163
00:13:38,840 --> 00:13:42,520
to appeal to older teens and working women

164
00:13:42,680 --> 00:13:45,000
who appreciate a premium aesthetic.

165
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,720
That fits Ratee's brief perfectly.

166
00:13:48,400 --> 00:13:49,200
Exactly!

167
00:13:49,640 --> 00:13:51,440
Just like Alice said. What do you think?

168
00:13:51,640 --> 00:13:52,640
Good idea, right?

169
00:13:53,760 --> 00:13:54,560
Makes sense, doesn't it?

170
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:57,120
It does.

171
00:13:57,160 --> 00:13:58,080
Slay, girl!

172
00:13:58,960 --> 00:13:59,760
Absolutely slay!

173
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:03,840
What?

174
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:05,720
I think these two are in for a long rivalry.

175
00:14:05,720 --> 00:14:07,400
They might become competitors

176
00:14:07,400 --> 00:14:10,400
for the title of our office's legendary content creator.

177
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:12,720
right here in our office, for sure.

178
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:15,480
Competitors? No way!

179
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:18,640
One works so hard she can barely breathe,

180
00:14:18,640 --> 00:14:19,880
while the other

181
00:14:20,080 --> 00:14:23,600
casually picks phone case colors from her shopping cart.

182
00:14:25,080 --> 00:14:25,880
Exactly.

183
00:14:26,400 --> 00:14:27,240
Um...

184
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:30,520
The afternoon campaign summary is done, Pim.

185
00:14:31,760 --> 00:14:33,240
Just put it down for now, Alice.

186
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:35,040
Take a break and drink some water.

187
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:37,600
You've been working nonstop since day one.

188
00:14:37,840 --> 00:14:42,280
Everyone here can see who's actually working.

189
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:44,000
You don't have to push yourself so hard.

190
00:14:45,160 --> 00:14:45,960
Okay.

191
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:52,760
Snacks!

192
00:14:53,640 --> 00:14:54,760
Thank you.

193
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:55,800
Thanks!

194
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:58,240
Can I have some too?

195
00:14:58,240 --> 00:14:59,600
Sharing is caring!

196
00:14:59,880 --> 00:15:01,800
You never miss a chance to eat, do you?

197
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:04,640
Never! Eating and gossiping go hand in hand.

198
00:15:05,400 --> 00:15:06,000
Stop it!

199
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,320
A break? We're allowed to rest?

200
00:15:07,920 --> 00:15:08,440
A break!

201
00:15:08,440 --> 00:15:08,960
A snack break.

202
00:15:09,160 --> 00:15:09,800
Let's work, shall we?

203
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:10,200
Okay.

204
00:15:10,200 --> 00:15:10,600
Sure.

205
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:12,560
Can I have one?

206
00:15:13,160 --> 00:15:13,680
Just one!

207
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:15,680
Sure.

208
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:38,600
Do you have that much free time, Alice?

209
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:40,320
Sorry?

210
00:15:40,840 --> 00:15:42,720
Why are you doing someone else's work?

211
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:46,800
Um...

212
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:48,200
Well...

213
00:15:57,240 --> 00:15:58,040
It's fine to be kind,

214
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:02,840
but you're not being very smart.

215
00:16:26,680 --> 00:16:28,680
Alice, we're heading home.

216
00:16:29,400 --> 00:16:30,440
Okay, bye-bye!

217
00:16:31,120 --> 00:16:31,920
Bye!

218
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:32,720
Bye-bye!

219
00:16:52,160 --> 00:16:53,360
Alice!

220
00:16:54,240 --> 00:16:56,360
Fun needs another favor.

221
00:16:56,760 --> 00:17:00,360
I didn't understand the campaign from this afternoon.

222
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:03,240
And I have to rush to dinner with my family.

223
00:17:03,480 --> 00:17:05,480
If I sit here trying to work it out alone,

224
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:08,520
I'll be late and get scolded for sure.

225
00:17:09,319 --> 00:17:10,400
Well, actually...

226
00:17:11,640 --> 00:17:15,839
I still haven't finished rescheduling our meetings

227
00:17:15,839 --> 00:17:17,319
or compiling the KOL list.

228
00:17:17,960 --> 00:17:20,359
Come on, please help me.

229
00:17:20,359 --> 00:17:21,720
It's just a little thing.

230
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:24,920
You can fix something this simple in no time, Alice.

231
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:27,240
I've already shared the file to your computer.

232
00:17:27,240 --> 00:17:30,040
I've got to go. Thanks, Alice! I'm counting on you!

233
00:17:51,920 --> 00:17:52,720
Hey!

234
00:17:53,760 --> 00:17:54,560
What is this?

235
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:59,880
The copy for the cosmetics campaign...

236
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:01,160
The content section?

237
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:03,840
You're doing someone else's work again, aren't you?

238
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:06,480
Yeah.

239
00:18:09,080 --> 00:18:10,880
But if I don't fix it,

240
00:18:11,520 --> 00:18:12,640
this whole project will be a disaster.

241
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:16,880
I can't just stand by and watch it fall apart.

242
00:18:18,920 --> 00:18:19,720
Listen.

243
00:18:21,960 --> 00:18:23,160
And if you're the one who falls apart,

244
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:24,360
who's going to help you?

245
00:18:26,280 --> 00:18:28,360
I know you're new here,

246
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:30,560
and you want to prove yourself.

247
00:18:31,280 --> 00:18:33,320
But your kindness

248
00:18:33,560 --> 00:18:35,080
is only going to ruin you.

249
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:36,080
Do you understand?

250
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:39,600
Now eat your dinner.

251
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,040
Can't I just finish a little more?

252
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:41,600
Hmph.

253
00:18:42,240 --> 00:18:43,040
That's enough.

254
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:54,240
Hey!

255
00:18:55,360 --> 00:18:56,200
What the hell?

256
00:18:56,200 --> 00:18:57,280
You look like you've seen a ghost.

257
00:18:58,640 --> 00:18:59,880
It's Nannalin!

258
00:19:00,120 --> 00:19:00,760
What about her?

259
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:03,040
She told me to come to her house.

260
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:04,600
Holy crap!

261
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:06,080
Don't say that!

262
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:09,160
Is she going to yell at me?

263
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:10,520
You're so screwed.

264
00:19:12,560 --> 00:19:13,360
Huh?

265
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:15,760
I really don't want to go.

266
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:32,400
I'm just dropping off work, Alice.

267
00:19:32,840 --> 00:19:33,960
It's no big deal.

268
00:20:12,560 --> 00:20:13,800
Come upstairs.

269
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,560
Or do I have to go down and get you myself?

270
00:20:45,800 --> 00:20:47,040
Um...

271
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:51,440
Does your house normally look like this, Ms. Nannalin?

272
00:20:52,120 --> 00:20:54,680
If I wasted all my time doing housework,

273
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:56,360
who would do tomorrow's work?

274
00:21:04,080 --> 00:21:04,880
And...

275
00:21:05,080 --> 00:21:07,280
Aren't you going to...

276
00:21:07,640 --> 00:21:09,400
clean up a little?

277
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:13,680
My regular housekeeper had to take sudden leave to go upcountry.

278
00:21:17,120 --> 00:21:18,680
Don't look at me like that.

279
00:21:25,600 --> 00:21:27,040
Just give me the documents.

280
00:23:02,840 --> 00:23:03,640
Alice.

281
00:23:05,760 --> 00:23:07,440
You really don't have to do that.

282
00:23:08,600 --> 00:23:09,920
It's not your job.

283
00:23:11,760 --> 00:23:12,640
It's okay.

284
00:23:28,080 --> 00:23:30,520
Who drinks this much tea every day?

285
00:23:31,280 --> 00:23:33,600
It keeps me from murdering people in meetings.

286
00:23:38,280 --> 00:23:40,640
Then please drink plenty of it.

287
00:24:30,640 --> 00:24:32,560
You're this flustered just seeing my underwear.

288
00:24:47,120 --> 00:24:48,560
If you saw me wearing it,

289
00:24:48,840 --> 00:24:51,200
would you have a heart attack, Alice?

290
00:25:15,880 --> 00:25:16,680
Am I beautiful?

291
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:20,560
Yes, you are.

292
00:25:24,920 --> 00:25:26,200
If I'm that beautiful,

293
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:30,320
are you just going to stand there?

294
00:25:34,320 --> 00:25:35,880
I don't want to just stand here.

295
00:32:11,360 --> 00:32:12,240
Tomorrow,

296
00:32:12,440 --> 00:32:15,160
don't take on Mueanfun's work again.

297
00:32:15,840 --> 00:32:18,240
I hired you to be my assistant,

298
00:32:19,240 --> 00:32:20,960
not a dumping ground

299
00:32:21,080 --> 00:32:22,920
for other people's responsibilities.

300
00:32:31,440 --> 00:32:32,520
If you do it again,

301
00:32:34,440 --> 00:32:35,280
I'll be angry.

302
00:32:43,880 --> 00:32:44,840
Okay.

303
00:32:46,040 --> 00:32:47,520
And next time,

304
00:32:48,640 --> 00:32:50,760
